  <data key="d5">In the case of RNA-seq data, a discrete Poisson kernel is employed: (2) F ^ r ( x ij ) = 1 n ∑ k = 1 n ∑ y = 0 x ij e − ( x ik + r ) ( x ik + r ) y y ! , where r =0.5 in order to set the mode of the Poisson kernel at each x i k , because the mode of a Poisson distribution with an integer mean λ occurs at λ and λ −1, and at the largest integer smaller than λ when λ is continuous.</data>
