  <data key="d5">Individuals were determined as phenotypic cases for a certain disease phenotype if they had at least two encounters for the corresponding Phecode diagnosis, while phenotypic controls consisted of individuals who never had the Phecode as well as those under Phecode exclusion criteria. Control group for acute renal failure, for instance, excluded acute renal failure, renal failure, chronic renal failure and several other related diseases of kidney and ureters (Phecodes ranging from 580 to 590.99).</data>
